UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): A detailed financial close checklist with reconciliation deadlines, review sign-offs, and completion tracking is a control activity under the COSO framework. Control activities are the policies and procedures that help ensure management directives are carried out, and this checklist establishes specific actions individuals must perform for accurate financial reporting.
Wrong (B): The control environment relates to the overall tone at the top, including integrity, ethical values, and governance structure — not specific procedural checklists.
Wrong (C): Monitoring activities involve evaluating internal control performance over time through ongoing or separate evaluations, not executing close procedures.
