-- Q1589: Audit Evidence [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 500.A31, evidence obtained directly from independent external sources — such as bank confirmations — is more reliable than evidence generated internally. The bank confirmation bypasses client personnel entirely, reducing the risk of manipulation or error.
Wrong (B): The controller''s printout is internally generated evidence under AU-C 500.A32, subject to the client''s internal control environment and therefore inherently less reliable than direct external confirmation.
Wrong (C): Although both reference the same bank balance, the manner of obtaining the evidence determines reliability — direct external confirmation is superior to a client-provided printout.
Wrong (D): Reconciliation to the general ledger tests internal consistency but does not make internally sourced evidence more reliable than an independent external confirmation.$EXPL$
