-- Q1592: Audit Evidence [medium/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 505.12, when positive confirmations are not returned after follow-up requests, the auditor should perform alternative procedures such as examining subsequent cash receipts, shipping documents, or sales contracts to obtain sufficient evidence about the assertions being tested.
Wrong (B): Assuming balances are correct based on the majority response rate violates AU-C 505.13, which states that non-responses do not constitute audit evidence.
Wrong (C): Non-responses alone do not automatically create a scope limitation warranting a qualified opinion — the auditor must first attempt alternative procedures.
Wrong (D): Sending unlimited additional requests and waiting indefinitely is impractical and not required by auditing standards; alternative procedures are the prescribed next step.$EXPL$
