-- Q1604: Audit Evidence [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under AU-C 540.18, if the auditor''s range does not include management''s point estimate, the difference between management''s estimate and the nearest end of the auditor''s range constitutes a misstatement. AU-C 540.19 requires the auditor to request that management revise the estimate, and if refused, the effect on the opinion is evaluated under AU-C 705.
Wrong (A): A qualified opinion is not automatic — the auditor first requests revision and evaluates materiality before determining the opinion impact.
Wrong (B): The estimate cannot be dismissed as immaterial simply because it falls outside the range; the difference itself must be evaluated for materiality.
Wrong (C): Expanding the auditor''s range to artificially include management''s estimate would undermine the purpose of developing an independent range.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1604;

