-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 500.A5, there is an inverse relationship between the quality (appropriateness) and quantity (sufficiency) of audit evidence. When evidence quality is high — such as evidence obtained directly from independent external sources — less quantity may be needed to achieve the required assurance level.
Wrong (B): Higher risk of material misstatement requires more evidence, not less. AU-C 330 requires increased audit effort in response to elevated risk assessments.
Wrong (C): Internal-source evidence is not always sufficient — reliability depends on the effectiveness of internal controls, and low-quality evidence cannot compensate for insufficient quantity.
Wrong (D): Professional judgment is central to determining both sufficiency and appropriateness under AU-C 500; it is not excluded from the evaluation process.$EXPL$
