-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under AU-C 540.A1 and AU-C 540.11, high estimation uncertainty exists when estimates depend on highly subjective assumptions about future conditions that are inherently unpredictable, such as long-term environmental liabilities or litigation outcomes. These estimates require significant auditor judgment and may give rise to significant risks.
Wrong (B): Estimates based on well-established actuarial tables with long track records have low estimation uncertainty because the inputs are objective and historically validated.
Wrong (C): Routine calculations using readily available market prices involve minimal subjectivity and therefore have low estimation uncertainty.
