-- Q1617: Audit Evidence [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under AU-C 560.14-15, when the auditor becomes aware of facts after the financial statements have been issued, the auditor should discuss the matter with management and, where appropriate, those charged with governance to determine whether revision is necessary and how management intends to address the matter.
Wrong (A): The auditor''s responsibility does not end upon issuance — AU-C 560.14 requires action when the auditor becomes aware of facts that may have caused a different report.
Wrong (C): Automatically reissuing the report with a new date is premature — the auditor must first assess the facts and determine whether revision of the financial statements is warranted.
Wrong (D): Directly notifying the regulatory agency without consulting management would bypass required professional procedures and the client relationship under AU-C 560.$EXPL$
