-- Q1624: Audit Evidence [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 450-20-25-2 (formerly SFAS 5), when a loss is probable and a range of amounts can be estimated but no single amount within the range is a better estimate, the entity accrues the minimum amount of the range (here, $2 million). The remainder of the range should be disclosed in the footnotes.
Wrong (A): Recording the maximum of $5 million would overstate the liability — ASC 450 requires the minimum of the range when no amount is more likely than another.
Wrong (B): Disclosure without accrual applies when a loss is reasonably possible, not when it is probable — a probable loss with an estimable range requires accrual.
Wrong (C): Recording the midpoint of $3.5 million is not required by ASC 450 — the standard specifically directs use of the minimum when no better estimate exists within the range.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 1624;
